From 01bac427ef85db4c8b4dcb227548959fef6f03fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: y-o-o-z <136268860+y-o-o-z@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:09:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] local: Inter and JetBrains Mono instead of Geist

The shellter theme now uses Inter (text and interface) and JetBrains Mono
(time, nick column, nick list, code), both SIL OFL 1.1 and hosted with the
theme: one variable file per subset (weights 100-900 / 100-800), latin +
latin-ext for Polish letters, italics only downloaded when italic text
appears. The nick list is monospaced too: in Inter "I" and "l" look the
same (124IA4IU3), in IRC nicks they are different characters, and 0/O are
told apart by JetBrains Mono's dotted zero. Programming ligatures (-> !=)
are off where IRC text is shown in JetBrains Mono. The fonts used from the
first frame are preloaded with the same URL as in the stylesheet.

Fonts: @fontsource-variable/inter 5.3.0, @fontsource-variable/jetbrains-mono
5.3.0; licenses in client/themes/shellter/fonts/OFL-*.txt.
